<title>PORTUGAL: BPI falls on BFE privatisation price.</title>
<headline>BPI falls on BFE privatisation price.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Portugues de Investimento fell sharply on news of its capital call to cover the purchase of Banco de Fomento &amp; Exterior, the state-controlled bank that is being privatised. But volume was thin.</p>
<p>BPI opened at 2,010 escudos and quickly retreated to around 1,950 escudos compared with the 2,115 escudos at which it stood before its suspension on August 23 when the government announced it would be taking over BPI.</p>
<p>Trade was only some 11,550 shares in the first few minutes.  </p>
<p>The bank announced a 60 billion escudo capital call to pay for the purchase of BFE.</p>
<p>It has yet to give details of the call.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
